hemlock@ucscb.UCSC.EDU (Strive-No-More) writes:

> I think it would still be a challenge if [color] dragon scale mail was
> permitted, and rings/amulets except for AOLS.  No object polymorphing.
> I eagerly await the first ascension post from someone with such equipment.

For me, the flaw in this concept of a limited-equipment ascension is
that the whole game of nethack radiates magic as it is - scrolls,
rings, wands, etc., not just shields of reflection and dragon scale
mail.  In "real" AD&D, I believe, non-mages aren't even allowed to use
such magical items as scrolls and wands.  Now, just try playing a game
without those!

The point is, I don't see anything wrong with exploiting every feature
of the game to your advantage (although I really don't like people
wishing for other class's quest item, but that's just personal).  I
think that even with using all the advantages the game is still a
challenge.

Of course, there's nothing wrong with setting limits to make the game
even more challenging; I'm just disputing the logic of excluding
certain magic items and not others.  The most interesting "limited"
game I saw someone mention here was a vegetarian character - someone
won with an elf without eating any corpses.  Now that is a neat
concept.

